      "message": "This will not work well as keys inside this array would be unretained and also you\u0027re leaking an array here!\n\nYou basically need to retain them one-by-one and return an autoreleased array.\n(you can check my implementation of allKeys for mutable dict as a reference)\n\nIn order to convince yourself you could write some tests similar to what I did to test allKeys for mutable dict:\n\n```\n    NSMutableDictionary *dict \u003d [NSMutableDictionary new];\n    for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c 5; i++) {\n        NSString *key \u003d [[NSString alloc] initWithFormat:@\"key %d\", i];\n        NSString *val \u003d [[NSString alloc] initWithFormat:@\"val %d\", i];\n        [dict setObject:val forKey:key];\n        [key release];\n        [val release];\n    }\n\n    NSArray *arr \u003d [dict allKeys];\n    [dict release];\n\n    for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c 5; i++) {\n        NSLog(@\"%@\", [arr objectAtIndex:i]);\n    }\n```\n\nP.S. you\u0027ll also need to unify allKeys methods of mutable and immutable dicts with some helper function to avoid code duplication",
